# Power button (2026-11-18/19, user's request): the keyboard's T16 - top row, last column, the orange power keycap.
# The keyboard microcontroller reads that optical key (also while the board is off: the keyboard is fed from
# VCC5V_BUS over its USB-C) and pulls PMIC_PWRON low over a 2-wire cable from the keyboard's J202 to J22 here, the way
# a PC's front-panel button reaches its motherboard.  The RK817's power-key logic is unchanged: a press switches the
# board on; while it runs a short press is a power-key event for the OS, about 6 s held cuts the power.
# J22 replaces the side-operated tact switch SW3; for bring-up or service, short J22's two pins (tweezers).
# (A panel-mount button in the codec cover was looked at first: no 12-19 mm one fits - 12 mm of room under the cover.)
SHEET pmic
J22 JST_SH2_PWR 1=PMIC_PWRON 2=GND
# the line leaves the board: ESD at the connector
ED13 ESD:BTR04G02 PMIC_PWRON GND
